    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.72) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18). **Kyle Tucker** represents our most compelling start despite a 37% rain risk; he faces Ryan Feltner, whose 5.05 xERA paired with a +14% park factor makes this an elite environment for power output. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** benefits from a high 19% SP skill adjustment against Robbie Ray, providing the best path for multi-category production. We are also leaning heavily on the favorable hitting environments at Coors Field and similar hitter-friendly parks, which have significantly bolstered the projections for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), **Heliot Ramos** (70.20), and **Andy Pages** (75.64). Notably, the slow delivery of opposing pitchers makes **Nasim Nunez** a sneakily effective start at 61.74, as his ability to capitalize on stolen base opportunities remains a priority for our roster construction.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed at a 53.91 rating but ultimately fell just short of the starting rotation. While the park factors and a strong 0.383 xwOBA suggest he is trending upward, the strength of the matchups for **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014who both benefit from a +16% park adjustment today\u2014pushed them ahead of him in the priority queue. We are also closely monitoring the lineup security for several players; because **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Andy Pages** are all \"Lineup Pending,\" our projected scores assume standard middle-of-the-pack slots. Should those lineups fluctuate downward, we will be ready to pivot, though we are currently confident in the upside provided by our current configuration of **Liam Hicks**, **Jackson Merrill**, and the rest of the squad.",
